# Dockerfile.worker uses `turbo prune --docker` (stage 1) to compute exactly which
# files matter, so this list is a coarse first pass — excluding the obviously-irrelevant
# bulk (node_modules, build output, git history) before that stage even runs, so the
# initial `COPY . .` into the pruner stage is fast and the build context isn't enormous.

node_modules
**/node_modules

.git
.gitignore

**/dist
**/.next
**/.turbo
**/coverage
**/generated

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

*.log
.DS_Store

.claude
.agents
.windsurf
plan/
docs/
README.md
